.TH P9SHARE-EXPORTS 5 "2026" "p9share" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
p9share-exports \- the directories a user shares with p9share
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I ~/.config/p9share/exports
has one share per line, three fields separated by white space:
.RS
.nf
DIR HOST NAME
.fi
.RE
.TP
.I DIR
An absolute path of the directory to share.  Letters, digits and  . _ + @ \- / only: no spaces or commas.
.TP
.I HOST
Where to send it, as
.BR ssh (1)
knows it (a name from ~/.ssh/config, or user@host).  ssh must work without a password.
.TP
.I NAME
A name for the share (letters, digits, . _ \-), unique in the file.  The receiving machine uses it too.
.PP
Blank lines and text after # are ignored.  The file is written by
.B p9share export
and
.BR "p9share unexport" ,
and may be edited by hand; a running
.B p9share serve
re-reads it every two seconds and starts, stops or restarts only the shares whose line changed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR p9share (8),
.BR p9share\-mounts (5)
